  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Attempted to cast Dragon Egg (a 0/2 defender) instead of the much more impactful Sarkhan, the Dragonspeaker. With Island as a land drop, the player would have 5 mana (2 Mountains, Thriving Bluff, 2 Islands) which is exactly enough for Sarkhan's {3}{R}{R} cost. Sarkhan could immediately +1 to become a 4/4 flying indestructible haste creature and start pressuring the opponent who has no creatures. Additionally, the mana plan for Dragon Egg was malformed, causing the payment to fail entirely.",
      "action_taken": "Attempted to cast Dragon Egg for {2}{R} (which failed due to mana payment error)",
      "better_line": "Play Island (land drop) first, then cast Sarkhan, the Dragonspeaker for {3}{R}{R} using Mountain, Mountain, Thriving Bluff, Island, Island. Activate +1 to become a 4/4 flying indestructible haste dragon and attack.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 98,
      "player": "MstMed Folksy",
      "decision_index": 25,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Failed to play Island from hand in postcombat main phase with 1 land drop remaining. This is a free action with no downside that provides crucial mana development. The player has Tolarian Kraken (6 mana) and Sarkhan (5 mana) in hand and needs every land drop. Missing this delays casting the Kraken by at least a turn.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without playing Island, ending the turn with an unspent land drop.",
      "better_line": "Play Island from hand to have 6 mana sources next turn, enabling Tolarian Kraken or Sarkhan + other plays.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 117,
      "player": "MstMed Folksy",
      "decision_index": 30,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Attempted to cast Sarkhan, the Dragonspeaker ({3}{R}{R}) before playing the Island from hand, resulting in insufficient mana and the cast being rolled back. With only 4 untapped lands (Island, 2 Mountains, Thriving Bluff) plus Unstable Obelisk, they needed to play the Island first to have enough mana sources.",
      "action_taken": "Attempted to cast Sarkhan, the Dragonspeaker without first making the available land drop, causing the spell to fail.",
      "better_line": "Play Island from hand first (increasing available mana to 6 sources), then cast Sarkhan, the Dragonspeaker with plenty of mana to pay {3}{R}{R}.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 146,
      "player": "MstMed Folksy",
      "decision_index": 35,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Attempted to cast Waterknot but the cast was rolled back due to insufficient blue mana (only 1 Island untapped, needed UU). Even if it had succeeded, the opponent has no creatures on board - only valid targets would be their own Goblin tokens. The failed attempt resulted in no action taken when productive plays were available.",
      "action_taken": "Attempted to cast Waterknot, which was rolled back by the game engine due to mana payment failure, resulting in no action.",
      "better_line": "Play Island (land drop) first, then cast Dragon Egg ({2}{R}) using Mountains/Obelisk/Bluff. This develops the board with a defensive creature that creates a 2/2 Dragon token when it dies, providing both defense and a future Dragon for synergies.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 160,
      "player": "MstMed Folksy",
      "decision_index": 38,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Attempted to cast Sarkhan, the Dragonspeaker ({3}{R}{R}) before playing a land, with only 4 untapped mana sources (needing 5 mana). The mana plan was also nonsensical, including the spell card itself as a mana source. The game rolled back the cast, wasting the priority window. The correct sequence was to play Island from hand first (using the available land drop), then cast Sarkhan with 5+ available mana.",
      "action_taken": "Attempted to cast Sarkhan, the Dragonspeaker with insufficient mana and without first making the land drop.",
      "better_line": "Play Island from hand first, then cast Sarkhan, the Dragonspeaker using Mountain + Mountain + Thriving Bluff + Island + Unstable Obelisk (or similar combination providing {3}{R}{R}).",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 177,
      "player": "MstMed Folksy",
      "decision_index": 43,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Player failed to take any action (timeout/failed cast) on a critical turn. With only 9 cards in library and opponent having Teferi's Tutelage actively milling them, the player needed to deploy threats immediately. Sarkhan, the Dragonspeaker was castable after playing an Island (giving 2 Mountains + Obelisk + Islands for {3}{R}{R}), and would have immediately attacked as a 4/4 flying indestructible creature against an empty board, dealing 4 to the opponent at 14 life.",
      "action_taken": "No action taken due to timeout/failed mana payment, effectively passing the entire turn.",
